WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.840
A D-Class prisoner enters the chamber. It is&nbsp;
quiet, save for the subtle whipping sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.520
coming from a bizarre shape in the middle of&nbsp;
the room. Upon closer inspection, it becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.760
clear that the floating object isn’t one entity,&nbsp;
but a mass of smaller objects, all floating and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.840
thrashing in the air. They’re ammunition, of&nbsp;
various calibers and sizes, spinning around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.840
in a spherical form. The D-class becomes nervous,&nbsp;
but is ordered to proceed by Foundation personnel.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.320
Slowly - inch by anxious inch - he advances&nbsp;
closer towards the mass of bullets...

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.600
His heart knocks harder against his chest with&nbsp;
every step he takes - the thumping begins to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.480
deafen his ears. He could feel his throat&nbsp;
tightening up as the blood rushes to his head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.160
and sweat starts to form on his brow. The sound&nbsp;
of the thrashing gets louder. With legs trembling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.120
and fingertips numbing, the D-class opens&nbsp;
his mouth in an attempt to let in a gasp of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.800
air to calm his nerves. But before he could even&nbsp;
take a full breath, and in the blink of an eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.440
countless bullets suddenly burst forth from&nbsp;
the mass, spraying the D-class relentlessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.640
with ammunition and killing him instantly. The&nbsp;
Foundation personnel watching this from safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.040
note down the events as they ponder the&nbsp;
question - why does this mass of living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:23.040
ammunition act so volatile? Why are some able&nbsp;
to approach it safely while others are killed?

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.840
What is the secret of SCP-577?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:33.840
Classified as Euclid, SCP-577 began as one of the&nbsp;
most mysterious objects in Foundation custody.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.240
An animated mass of ammunition, those who were&nbsp;
able to get close enough to it observed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.960
the plurality of the bullets inside were&nbsp;
9mm, accompanied by a selection of 10mm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.360
and .45 rounds. The bullets are normally&nbsp;
calm, moving in predictable patterns and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.240
occasionally shifting the mass to reflect&nbsp;
other shapes, including cats and dogs.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.480
But something else about the mass&nbsp;
concerns the Foundation much more.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.040
The mass is growing. It is dramatically&nbsp;
larger than it was when it was first acquired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.000
by the Foundation, and seems to be adding&nbsp;
approximately a thousand bullets per year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.320
This raises the question - can it&nbsp;
be contained permanently? Currently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:17.120
it is held in a standard large containment unit,&nbsp;
but it's quarters have been reinforced with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.720
Foundation’s best steel blast shielding. Due&nbsp;
to the danger to anyone who opens the door, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.400
entire facility is handled with remote technology&nbsp;
and can only be opened by approved personnel.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.440
But someone needs to check&nbsp;
that everything is stable.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.560
The Foundation learned the hard way that&nbsp;
entering the containment unit was a bad idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.240
Any Foundation staff, ranging from a high-level&nbsp;
scientist to a standard security officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.160
is met with immediate hostility from SCP-577’s&nbsp;
mass of bullets the second they approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.640
the entity. The bullets shoot out from the&nbsp;
mass with the speed of a standard handgun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.400
aiming directly at their target. This&nbsp;
indicates that SCP-577 is intelligent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:04.560
it is capable of seeing and reacting - and&nbsp;
it hates Foundation personnel with a passion.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.880
Fortunately, the Foundation doesn’t&nbsp;
have to sacrifice it’s permanent staff.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.880
SCP-577 is not the first entity to react with&nbsp;
hostility toward its captors - after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.440
few of the specimens are happy to be&nbsp;
permanently contained in secure facilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.840
So it was determined that D-class personnel&nbsp;
would be sent into the facility twice a year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.120
to inspect it for any damage, make sure&nbsp;
the entity was still secure - and test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:35.280
SCP-577’s reaction to the presence of different&nbsp;
people not from the Foundation’s staff.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.080
And that’s where things got interesting.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.360
Many of the D-class personnel didn’t trigger the&nbsp;
entity at all, resulting in neutral behavior.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.760
However, those D-class who were initially&nbsp;
Foundation staff and demoted due to broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:53.840
policy were met with the same hostility as&nbsp;
current staff - indicating that SCP-577 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:59.280
not going to be fooled easily. The same happened&nbsp;
with some D-class with a specific background,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.000
who were immediately sprayed with a violent&nbsp;
hail of bullets, causing injury or death.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.680
Upon investigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.200
every single one of those D-Class was revealed&nbsp;
to previously be a member of law enforcement.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.280
However, some D-class personnel were&nbsp;
met with a very different reaction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.880
These people were the most likely to see&nbsp;
the other side of SCP-577, when it reduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.400
its hostile stance and instead took on a&nbsp;
friendly form. Appearing as a dog or cat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.000
it would even approach the D-class&nbsp;
in a welcoming manner. This was most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.280
likely to happen when the D-class was formerly&nbsp;
homeless or had spent time in the prison system.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.800
But one incident brought SCP-577’s&nbsp;
true nature into a new light.&nbsp;

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:48.800
D-28126 was the latest unfortunate conscript to be&nbsp;
sent into SCP-577’s chamber for an annual cleaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.840
and inspection. His duties were simple,&nbsp;
including to inspect the walls for damage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.600
clean out any stray material left&nbsp;
around by the bullets firing - as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.880
well as any corpses that were left behind&nbsp;
- and make any needed repairs to the walls.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.200
He would be wearing protective gear, but that&nbsp;
wasn’t always enough to protect someone from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.640
the hail of bullets - and no one knew exactly&nbsp;
how the volatile mass of bullets would react.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:18.880
But from the second the D-class entered, it was&nbsp;
clear this would be a very different encounter.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:26.400
As soon as D-28126 entered, SCP-577 seemed to&nbsp;
take on a friendly posture. It shape-shifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.520
into the form of a large cat, and would frequently&nbsp;
approach the D-class while he was cleaning. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:37.200
D-class was confused at first, but soon seemed to&nbsp;
appreciate the company. He would occasionally stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:43.280
cleaning to pet the cat made out of bullets, but&nbsp;
as the work went on, he seemed to slow down. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.560
appeared to be crying, and eventually he stopped&nbsp;
working entirely and slumped against the wall.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.200
The Foundation attempted communication&nbsp;
with him, but the D-class didn’t respond.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.960
Soon, SCP-577 joined him against the wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.200
and the D-class held him. His hand&nbsp;
was guided into the mass of bullets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.640
and it soon emerged holding a single bullet.&nbsp;
The D-class held the strange entity for a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.240
more minutes, before the staff’s insistence that&nbsp;
he exit the chamber grew stronger. He eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.960
left, and the Foundation took him back into&nbsp;
custody and examined the bullet he was holding.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.440
It was NOT a normal bullet.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:24.800
The bullet was moving, almost as if it was&nbsp;
a beating heart as it throbbed up and down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:31.040
Upon closer inspection, it was revealed to be&nbsp;
covered with blood - but D-28126 had not been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:36.400
hit by the bullet. He was completely uninjured,&nbsp;
but when he emerged from the chamber his hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.600
was covered in blood - exactly where he&nbsp;
had inserted it into the mass of bullets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.840
The bullet was sent to SCP facilities for&nbsp;
testing. The blood was not a match for D-28126.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.080
But it was genetically similar - like a relative.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.720
The D-class was brought back to the interrogation&nbsp;
chamber, and the bullet was returned to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:04.480
He was apparently linked to SCP-577 somehow, and&nbsp;
identified himself by his name - Arturo Rojas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.680
His interviewer, Dr. Vanderbilt, asked him to&nbsp;
explain what happened, and Arturo explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:15.440
that the mass of bullets didn’t just turn into&nbsp;
a cat - it turned into a cat he knew as a child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:19.520
which had a uniquely shaped tail&nbsp;
that he would recognize anywhere.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:23.360
The cat that was once helped&nbsp;
by Arturo...and his brother.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.000
Arturo was questioned why he quit working&nbsp;
and began crying, and revealed that he heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:35.600
the mass of bullets say something, barely&nbsp;
audible. SCP-577 had whispered “I’m sorry”.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.320
But what would a cat have to be sorry for?

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.440
Arturo became angry when Dr.&nbsp;
Vanderbilt questioned this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.080
but Dr. Vanderbilt continued and conceded&nbsp;
that Arturo recognized the cat somehow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:50.480
He prodded Arturo to share the rest of the&nbsp;
story - and Arturo eventually revealed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:57.520
root of his bond to SCP-577. Arturo and his deaf&nbsp;
brother Ricardo were homeless at a young age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.240
after their mother threw them out. While they&nbsp;
were living on the streets, they met a cat that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:07.360
they gave a little of their food to from time&nbsp;
to time. The little cat became their constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.880
companion. They named him Duck, after Arturo’s&nbsp;
brother’s favorite sign language gesture.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.840
But tragedy was just around the corner.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.280
Duck and Ricardo were inseparable, with the little&nbsp;
cat essentially becoming a therapy pet to the boy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:25.600
But one day, Ricardo encountered a police&nbsp;
officer. The deaf boy couldn’t understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:30.480
the officer’s orders, and the officer didn’t&nbsp;
know or didn’t bother to use sign language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.920
Ultimately bullets were fired. Ricardo was&nbsp;
killed, another unarmed young man killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:41.680
in a police shooting, and Duck was left&nbsp;
alone. But the cat had one more job to do.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.160
He had to lead Arturo back to his brother.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:49.360
The area was swarming with police, and Arturo&nbsp;
never got a chance to say goodbye. He lashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:54.320
out at the only one he could - Duck. The&nbsp;
cat tried to comfort his surviving person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:59.040
but Arturo threw rocks at the cat and&nbsp;
chased him away. He never saw the cat again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.200
and was left alone with his grief. He saw&nbsp;
on the news days later that the officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:07.200
was cleared in the shooting, his brother&nbsp;
was blamed for threatening the officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.400
and the news implied that Ricardo was a gang&nbsp;
member. Arturo was left without closure.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:16.240
Until SCP-577 entered the picture.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.040
Dr. Vanderbilt expressed his sympathies,&nbsp;
but wasn’t sure what any of this had to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:26.480
with the entity. Arturo explained further why he&nbsp;
started crying when he felt the pulsating bullet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:31.360
He had spent years sleeping next to Ricardo&nbsp;
- and he recognized his brother’s heartbeat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:37.040
The bullet was his brother’s heart, or at least&nbsp;
contained his essence. And for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:42.640
in ten years, Arturo was able to make peace not&nbsp;
just with the cat he had rejected out of grief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:46.000
but with the brother he had lost far too young.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.840
The Foundation had answers - but&nbsp;
they only led to more questions.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:56.320
Arturo had pulled a single bullet out of the&nbsp;
mass of SCP-577 - and it was the one containing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:01.200
his brother’s heart. Was this the bullet that&nbsp;
killed Ricardo? Was every bullet in the mass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:07.040
one that killed a person? Was the mass growing&nbsp;
with every new death? And if that was the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.080
did the mass contain the combined memory -&nbsp;
and pain - of every life a bullet took? If so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:16.720
that would explain the compassion the entity&nbsp;
seems to hold for those who have been homeless or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:22.240
imprisoned - as well as its intense hostility&nbsp;
for any sort of law enforcement figure.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:27.280
For now, SCP-577 remains stable&nbsp;
and contained within its unit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:33.360
needing only standard upkeep of its cell to&nbsp;
avoid any breaches. But as it continues to grow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.840
Foundation authorities worry that it may get&nbsp;
strong enough to eventually breach containment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:43.040
But this is a tricky case for the Foundation.&nbsp;
The entity’s growth is out of their control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:48.480
and nothing they’ve done to date has stopped or&nbsp;
slowed it in any way. It seems something on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:54.880
outside is making it grow, and it shows&nbsp;
no sign of slowing down any time soon.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.280
For another SCP with a benevolent side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:03.280
check out “SCP-2295 - The Bear with a Heart&nbsp;
of Patchwork”, or watch this video instead.

